# Tauri 2 dev-watcher exclude list. Patterns here are NOT triggered for
# rebuild during `tauri dev`. Per Tauri 2 docs `.taurignore` follows
# `.gitignore` syntax.
#
# Why this exists:
# pulse-app/src/main.rs production router calls `taurpc::Router::new()
# .export_config(taurpc_export_config()).into_handler()` which writes
# `ui/src/bindings/index.ts` at every binary launch. Without this exclude,
# Tauri's dev watcher fires on the auto-regenerated file → kills the app
# → rebuilds → new binary regenerates again → infinite HMR loop. The
# binary itself boots cleanly; only dev-mode usability is broken.
#
# Bindings are regenerated on demand via:
#   cargo nextest run -p pulse-app emit_taurpc_bindings
#
# (see `pulse-app/src/main.rs::tests::emit_taurpc_bindings`).

ui/src/bindings/
